# 1. What Are Cookies

Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you use a website or app, used to remember information about your visit.

# 2. Cookies We Use

| **Category** | **Purpose** | **Can You Opt Out?** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Strictly Necessary / Session | Keeps you logged in and your session secure while using the platform. | No — required for the platform to function. |
| Functional | Remembers preferences such as your CAT-LOC-VAL discovery filters, so you don't have to reset them each visit. | Yes, though some convenience features may not work without them. |
| Analytics | Helps us understand how the platform is used, to improve it over time. | Yes, where offered. |

*[Drafting note: this table reflects a standard cookie taxonomy, not a confirmed technical decision. No analytics or marketing tooling has been formally selected as part of this platform**'**s build to date (unlike Auth0, Gemini, or SabPaisa, which were explicit vendor decisions) — this Policy should be finalised only once the actual analytics stack, if any, is chosen, since the specific tools used must be named here for the Policy to be accurate.]*

# 3. What We Do Not Use Cookies For

- We do not use cookies to store your banking details, EMD/deposit balance, or KYC documents — this data is held server-side, within our segregated escrow and encrypted storage systems, never in a browser cookie.

- We do not use third-party advertising or ad-retargeting cookies.

# 4. Third-Party Cookies

**4.1. **Our Payment Gateway partner (SabPaisa) may set its own cookies during the payment/checkout process, governed by their own cookie and privacy practices, not this Policy.

*[Drafting note: confirm directly with SabPaisa what cookies, if any, their checkout flow sets, so this section can be stated precisely rather than generically.]*

# 5. Managing Your Preferences

**5.1. **Most browsers let you block or delete cookies through their settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies will prevent you from using core platform features, including logging in.

# 6. Changes to This Policy

**6.1. **We may update this Policy as our use of cookies changes. Material changes will be reflected in the "Effective Date" above.

